 down to stop stop  the market decline I have not had that  conversation with any of those groups I  talked about that they're not  considering it at Treasury at Congress  in any of those areas and I think that  that understanding that that's not the  case would be actually be helpful to  investor sentiment if people here the  market might be closed they may be more  inclined to sell if they're afraid they  won't be - and that's right so I think  hearing a clear statement which we have  heard from secretary minutiae and we  have heard from chairman Clayton at the  SES they have no plans to close the  market you're hearing it from me the  markets are staying open we're talking  about closing the markets we're not  talking about shortening the trading day  repeating that message I think is really  important for everyone to hear Stacy  thank you we will see you soon  appreciate it very much
 

